---
import { createLocalBusiness } from 'astro-aeo/schema';
const business = createLocalBusiness({
  '@id': 'https://recipe.example.com/#bakery',
  name: 'Harbor Street Bakery',
  telephone: '+49 30 0000000',
});
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({ '@context': 'https://schema.org', ...business });
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Harbor Street Bakery: Bread Baked Every Morning</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Sourdough, rye and pastries, baked daily on Harbor Street." />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Harbor Street Bakery: Bread Baked Every Morning" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Sourdough, rye and pastries, baked daily on Harbor Street." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://recipe.example.com/og.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Harbor Street Bakery: Bread Baked Every Morning</h1>
      <p>This recipe page carries enough plain prose for a useful Markdown companion. It explains what the page is for, who it helps, and what a reader can do next, in ordinary sentences an answer engine can quote. Replace this text with your own content and keep each page focused on one question.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
